1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,634
In my view, there has been no breakthrough
and no serious progress in the

2
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:21,000
negotiations so far.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The war will continue.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,820
I wrote on my Telegram channel that, as
I have already explained, Medinsky is

5
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:38,000
not a figure whose presence
signals serious intent.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
“Stall for time, Shura, stall for time.” That's
how I described what happened in Abu Dhabi.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,087
Now, if you'll allow me, I'm going to
put your nerves, your eyes and ears to a

8
00:00:56,087 --> 00:00:59,000
serious test, my friends.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,333
Forgive me, please, but I have to do
this for the sake of objectivity. We're

10
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:07,000
now, I almost said for the first time—

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,228
No, not for the first time, of course—going
to behold the propagandist of all

12
00:01:13,228 --> 00:01:18,000
Rus', Vladimir Rudolfovich
Solovyov, also known as Shapiro.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:27,625
I'll explain later why I want to show
you this man, who also commented on the

14
00:01:27,625 --> 00:01:32,000
presence of Europeans at the talks.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,878
They wanted to attend. Some even flew
to Abu Dhabi, but they weren't allowed

16
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:37,000
into the negotiations.

17
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:47,000
And Solovyov is also trying to comment on
what happened with his usual rudeness.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,382
I almost said a swear word. Let's
listen to Solovyov. Let us summon our

19
00:01:53,382 --> 00:01:55,000
patience, friends.

20
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:59,600
NATO is fighting us and losing. [inaudible]

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,452
Ursula von der Leyen says: “We will
negotiate a new security architecture only

22
00:02:05,452 --> 00:02:07,200
after there is a freeze.”

23
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:12,000
There will be no freeze, you
fool. We don't need a freeze.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,047
Are we asking for a ceasefire? Are we
asking for an end to the fighting? Do we

25
00:02:18,047 --> 00:02:22,000
want to stop the war? We
want to achieve our goals,

26
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,500
and we are ready to pursue them both
diplomatically and militarily if

27
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:28,000
diplomacy doesn't work.

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,500
We do not say our goal is to end the
war. We entered these hostilities to end

29
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:36,000
the war against the Russian people.

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
We prevented another June 22, 1941. It
was a difficult but necessary decision.

31
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
There you have it, my friends: “a
difficult but necessary decision.”

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Forgive me again for making you look at that
face. I'll explain why I played this clip.

33
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:08,866
Solovyov makes it clear that the Russian
side will continue fighting until its

34
00:03:08,866 --> 00:03:12,000
conditions are met.

35
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:20,955
We understand perfectly well that
achieving the conditions President Putin

36
00:03:20,955 --> 00:03:31,000
stated on February 24, 2022, is extremely
difficult for Russia in its current state.

37
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:37,111
Let's hope the situation doesn't swing
in the opposite direction. But I wrote

38
00:03:37,111 --> 00:03:41,000
on my Telegram channel
about Solovyov's rhetoric.

39
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:47,160
He insults Europe in every possible way.
I'm not whitewashing Europe; God can

40
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,000
judge those people too.

41
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,116
Things aren't so clear-cut there either,
and their hands aren't clean. But

42
00:03:52,116 --> 00:04:02,000
that's not the point. The point is that
Solovyov is relaying what he is told to relay.

43
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:09,000
He conveys our country's position to
its people: the war will continue.

44
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:16,000
I wrote on my Telegram channel, commenting on
Solovyov's claim that NATO had lost to us:

45
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:24,000
“Yes, wonderful, NATO has lost to us. Citizen
Solovyov, NATO hasn't entered the war yet.”

46
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Remember the reverse situation? Everything
comes back: the boomerang principle.

47
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:35,715
During the events in Donbas, when people
shouted, “The Russian army is there,”

48
00:04:35,715 --> 00:04:42,000
our side kept saying, “The Russian
army hasn't even entered the war yet.”

49
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,204
That was one of Russian propaganda's
favorite lines: the Russian army hadn't

50
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:50,000
even started fighting.

51
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Now one could say much the same about
NATO. Are they supplying weapons? Yes.

52
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Are there instructors there? Yes.

53
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Are there possibly separate groups, such as
sabotage and reconnaissance units? Possibly.

54
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:13,000
It is a mirror image of the situation in
Donbas in 2014. An absolute mirror image.

55
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Are there volunteers from
NATO countries? Yes.

56
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Wasn't there a similar situation
in 2014? It's all the same.

57
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:28,000
So why get hysterical about NATO
losing? NATO hasn't even started.

58
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:35,400
If citizen Solovyov talked to the
military, to senior officers, they would

59
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,000
quickly explain it to him.

60
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:46,000
As I've said many times, how long would
we last in a full-scale, non-nuclear

61
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
conflict with NATO?

62
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Consider the current state of our army,
from ammunition to the people in command.

63
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:04,000
The General Staff, starting with Gerasimov
and down through his inner circle.

64
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Consider the economic situation in
our country and the social situation,

65
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:20,000
with society deeply divided. Consider,
too, the Russian armed forces:

66
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:31,000
the soldiers and officers are exhausted.
They've been in the trenches for five years.

67
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,878
They have completely exhausted their
human resources, and no rotation or

68
00:06:36,878 --> 00:06:39,000
replacements are in sight,

69
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:46,000
because we understand perfectly well that
mobilization could trigger a social explosion.

70
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:56,000
And given all that, citizen Solovyov
believes Russian society, tired of war,

71
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:02,000
will eagerly rush to fight fresh
NATO divisions armed to the teeth.

72
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:09,684
Or perhaps citizen Solovyov thinks
North Korea will provide Russia with a

73
00:07:09,684 --> 00:07:16,000
million fresh, energetic North
Korean soldiers and officers.

74
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:21,797
I'm simply curious how citizen Solovyov
imagines a serious military conflict

75
00:07:21,797 --> 00:07:25,000
with NATO under the current circumstances.

76
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:31,083
Solovyov, just like Medinsky, is part
of the same story: “Stall for time,

77
00:07:31,083 --> 00:07:33,000
Shura, stall for time.”

78
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:43,000
I could understand buying time if a major
reorganization of the army were underway,

79
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:51,000
if the economy were being reorganized and
there had been a revolution in personnel,

80
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:58,000
with equivalents of Stalin's old
people's commissars now in government.

81
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:05,000
If all that were happening, I could
understand why they were stalling:

82
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:15,000
to gain time to reorganize the
state, from the army to the economy.

83
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,324
But nothing is changing. The same people
run the army and the economy; there's

84
00:08:21,324 --> 00:08:24,000
no personnel revolution in sight.

85
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:29,000
It's all useless; the same old
faces are still in the ring.

86
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:36,000
So what's the point of
stalling? I shared my view:

87
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:45,553
the point is that while the current
situation persists and the war

88
00:08:45,553 --> 00:08:47,000
continues,

89
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:57,000
there is still no serious basis for saying
that the Russian Federation in this conflict

90
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:03,000
has won a substantial victory or gained
something it can present to the public,

91
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,139
saying, “Look, dear Russians, this
is what you suffered for, what we

92
00:09:07,139 --> 00:09:10,000
sacrificed hundreds of
thousands of people for,

93
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:14,000
what all this happened
for. This is the reason.”

94
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Until there is something to
show for the whole undertaking,

95
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:26,000
stopping the war could
mean for those in power

96
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:30,000
the beginning of very serious problems,

97
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
potentially fatal problems.

98
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
And I think they understand
that perfectly well.

99
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Even though they live in a land of pink
ponies, they understand perfectly well that,

100
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:51,000
in the current circumstances, with
the conflict in its present state,

101
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
stopping it carries risks.

102
00:09:54,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Perhaps that's why we hear the rhetoric I
jokingly called “Stall for time, Shura.”

103
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:07,000
What are they hoping for? I can't say.

104
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Again, I see no serious reason to believe
our country will be transformed soon.

105
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:21,000
On the contrary, I see reasons to think it
will sink deeper and deeper into problems.

106
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
There is another way out of this situation.

107
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
I mean a full-scale conflict with NATO.

108
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Putin, incidentally, spoke
quite clearly about this.

109
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,438
He said, roughly speaking, that we
understand the two sides are in very

110
00:10:34,438 --> 00:10:36,000
different weight classes.

111
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:43,903
And that could, on the contrary, prompt
us to use nuclear weapons from the

112
00:10:43,903 --> 00:10:47,000
very beginning of a conflict.

113
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,000
In other words, we're talking
about a nuclear apocalypse.

114
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:56,000
I wonder: is citizen Solovyov
ready for a nuclear apocalypse?

115
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
I'm not ready. I'm not ready.

116
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:03,000
I don't want a nuclear winter
for planet Earth, I'm sorry.

117
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:08,000
I don't think you're ready for a
nuclear apocalypse or want one either.

118
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
And patriotism has no role to play here.

119
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Billions of people on our
planet aren't ready for it.

120
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:24,440
Therefore, I sincerely hope the situation
will be resolved in a different way.
